<title>GERMANY: Tarkett wins U.S. approval in Allibert deal.</title>
<headline>Tarkett wins U.S. approval in Allibert deal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKENTHAL, Germany 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German floor covering firm Tarkett AG said on Tuesday it had won approval from U.S. regulatory authorities for its merger with France's Sommer Allibert.</p>
<p>Tarkett plans to merge its floor covering business with Sommer Allibert to create Tarkett-Sommer AG, which would become one of the world leaders in this segment with annual sales of 2.6 billion marks, 27 plants worldwide and 8,800 employees.</p>
<p>Rival American firm Armstrong World Industries, had sought to block the merger deal.</p>
<p>Tarkett said it was now seeking merger approval from German authorities.</p>
<p>The merger deal, announced in May, involves Sommer-Allibert taking a 60 percent stake in Tarkett in a deal valuing Tarkett shares at 32.75 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
